#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md:6
msgid "Typestate Pattern: Problem"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md:8
msgid ""
"How can we ensure that only valid operations are allowed on a value based on "
"its current state?"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md:12
msgid "// Copyright 2025 Google LLC\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md:13
msgid "// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md:24
msgid "\"{name} {{\""
msgstr "\"{name} {{\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md:28
msgid "\"  {key}={value};\""
msgstr "\"  {key}={value};\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md:32
msgid "\"}\\n\""
msgstr "\"}\\n\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md:42
msgid "\"User\""
msgstr "\"User\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md:43
msgid "\"id\""
msgstr "\"id\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md:43
msgid "\"42\""
msgstr "\"42\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md:44
msgid "\"name\""
msgstr "\"name\""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md:44
msgid "\"Alice\""
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md:46
msgid "// serializer.serialize_struct_end(); // ← Oops! Forgotten\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md:48
msgid "\"{}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md:55
msgid "This `Serializer` is meant to write a structured value."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md:57
msgid ""
"However, in this example we forgot to call `serialize_struct_end()` before "
"`finish()`. As a result, the serialized output is incomplete or "
"syntactically incorrect."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md:61
msgid ""
"One approach to fix this would be to track internal state manually, and "
"return a `Result` from methods like `serialize_struct_field()` or `finish()` "
"if the current state is invalid."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md:65
msgid "But this has downsides:"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md:67
msgid ""
"It is easy to get wrong as an implementer. Rust’s type system cannot help "
"enforce the correctness of our state transitions."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md:70
msgid ""
"It also adds unnecessary burden on the user, who must handle `Result` values "
"for operations that are misused in source code rather than at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md:73
msgid ""
"A better solution is to model the valid state transitions directly in the "
"type system."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/typestate-pattern.md:76
msgid ""
"In the next slide, we will apply the **typestate pattern** to enforce "
"correct usage at compile time and make it impossible to call incompatible "
"methods or forget to do a required action."
msgstr ""
